# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` package using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with dependency resolution

### 2. Code Configuration
- Modified `client/src/App.jsx`:
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<BrowserRouter>` component at the root level

### 3. Framework-Specific Details
- Project Framework: React with Vite
- Package Import: `@vercel/speed-insights/react` (as per official documentation for React apps)
- Component Placement: Added to the root App component, inside BrowserRouter to ensure it's present on all routes

## Implementation Approach

1. **Documentation Research**: Fetched the latest installation instructions from the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart)

2. **Framework Detection**: Identified the project as a React + Vite application by examining:
   - `client/package.json` (contains React and Vite dependencies)
   - `client/vite.config.js` (Vite configuration)
   - `client/src/main.jsx` (React entry point)

3. **Installation**: Followed the official documentation's React-specific instructions:
   - Used npm to install the package
   - Imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/react` for standard React applications
   - Placed the component at the application root level

4. **Component Placement**: Added `<SpeedInsights />` inside the `<BrowserRouter>` component in App.jsx, ensuring it's included on all routes of the application

## Verification

✅ Package successfully installed (174 packages added)
✅ Build completed successfully (vite build passed)
✅ No new linting errors introduced (pre-existing linting issues in codebase are unrelated to these changes)
✅ No test suite available to run
✅ Lock files properly updated

## Files Modified

- `client/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `client/package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `client/src/App.jsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel, the Speed Insights tracking will automatically begin collecting performance metrics. No additional configuration is required for basic functionality.

## Notes

- The Speed Insights component is lightweight and will only activate when the application is deployed on Vercel
- Performance data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section
- The component placement ensures tracking across all routes of the application
